{"name":"Flower Field","hex":"#d9a96f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorful, conspicuous structure associated with angiosperms, frequently scented and attracting various insects, and which may or may not be used for sexual reproduction.","A reproductive structure in angiosperms (flowering plants), often conspicuously colourful and typically including sepals, petals, and either or both stamens and/or a pistil."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put forth blooms.","To decorate with pictures of flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower"},{"term":"field","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A land area free of woodland, cities, and towns; an area of open country.","The open country near or belonging to a town or city."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To intercept or catch (a ball) and play it.","To be the team catching and throwing the ball, as opposed to hitting it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/field"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower","wikidata":"Q506"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg/500px-Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg/1280px-Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg/500px-Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhalaenopsis_bellina_(Blue_Pink_x_sib)_(Rchb.f.)_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_(1995)._20210623_013709.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG/500px-Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG/1280px-Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG/500px-Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunflower_from_Silesia.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Passiflora_caerulea_%28makro_close-up%29.